ComponentTypeController ..> ComponentTypeData
ComponentTypeController ..> ComponentTypeSearchDTO
ComponentTypeService --> IComponentTypeRepository
ComponentTypeService --> IUnitOfWork
ComponentTypeService --> IComponentTypeImpactGuard
ComponentTypeService --> ComponentTypeResponseMapper
ComponentTypeService ..> ComponentTypeSearchCriteria
IComponentTypeRepository ..> ComponentTypeSearchCriteria
ComponentTypeService ..> PizzaComponentType
ComponentTypeResponseMapper ..> PizzaComponentType
ComponentTypeResponseMapper ..> ComponentTypeResponseDTO
PizzaComponentType "1" *-- "1" ComponentTypeId
PizzaComponentType "1" *-- "1" ComponentTypeName
Product "0..*" --> "0..1" PizzaComponentType : classified by
PostgresComponentTypeRepository ..|> IComponentTypeRepository
PostgresUnitOfWork ..|> IUnitOfWork
PostgresUnitOfWork --> Database
PostgresComponentTypeRepository --> Database
note bottom of ComponentTypeUpdateDTO
 Omitted fields retain their current values.
 Explicit maxQuantity = null removes the upper bound.
 Only maxQuantity accepts null; ? denotes an optional field.
 The complete resulting state is validated before saving.
end note
note bottom of PizzaComponentType
 min >= 0; finite max >= min; null = unbounded.
 revised() returns a validated candidate with the same ID.
 Order uniqueness is a set-wide rule enforced at persistence.
end note
note bottom of IComponentTypeRepository
 Postgres adapter implements all operations shown here.
 Search uses domain-owned criteria, independent of HTTP
 and application DTOs.
end note
note bottom of Product
 Exactly one type when isPizzaComponent = true;
 otherwise none. No ownership or cascade deletion.
end note
legend bottom
 Interfaces denote injected JavaScript contracts.
endlegend
